.TH CHTTP_BASE64_DECODE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_decode \- decode a base64 string (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

void *chttp_base64_decode(const char *b64_input, size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a static inline wrapper that calls chttp_base64_decode_mp()
with NULL memory management procedures, so it allocates with malloc.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
b64_input  The NUL-terminated base64 string to decode. It must not
           be NULL.
out_len    Optional. It receives the number of decoded bytes. Pass
           NULL if you don't need it.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new buffer with the decoded bytes on success.
NULL if the allocation fails or the input is malformed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_decode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode (3)
